WebAssembly build fixes for GNU APL svn trunk (verified at r2091).

1) libapl.cc fix_function_NL(): wrap Quad_FX::do_quad_FX() in try/catch like
   apl_exec() already is upstream. A header that makes ⎕FX throw (e.g. a
   lambda-style 'λ←f ⍵', which raises DEFN ERROR) otherwise escapes across
   extern "C" as an uncaught C++ exception and kills the embedding host.
2) libapl.cc set_value(): Cell::init(src, owner, loc) no longer exists; the
   trunk API is src.init_other(dest, owner, loc). libapl is rarely built
   upstream, so it drifts against the core headers.
3) Quad_FIO.cc: qualify the socket bind() as ::bind(). Common.hh puts
   'using namespace std' in scope, and under emscripten's libc headers the
   unqualified call resolves to std::bind and fails to compile.
4) rval.def + Quad_RVAL.cc: the stimulus fields contained bare ¯ (U+00AF)
   tokens which the prim_def macro stringified; LLVM 23 rejects U+00AF as a
   preprocessing token outside literals. The fields are now string literals
   and the macro no longer stringifies - the stored table is byte-identical.

patches/wasm-stubs.c (linked, not patched): sem_timedwait() returning ENOSYS,
referenced by Quad_PLOT.hh; a browser has no plot windows to wait for.

